# Description

The `module.exports` statement in `backend/routes/api/comments.js` was placed before route definitions, inconsistent with all other route files (`users.js`, `profiles.js`, `tags.js`, `items.js`, `ping.js`).

Moved `module.exports = router;` from line 37 to the end of the file (line 60), after all route definitions.

**Before:**
```javascript
const router = require("express").Router();
const mongoose = require("mongoose");
const Comment = mongoose.model("Comment");

module.exports = router;  // ← Exported before routes defined

router.get("/", async (req, res) => {
  // ...
});

router.delete("/:commentId", async (req, res) => {
  // ...
});
```

**After:**
```javascript
const router = require("express").Router();
const mongoose = require("mongoose");
const Comment = mongoose.model("Comment");

router.get("/", async (req, res) => {
  // ...
});

router.delete("/:commentId", async (req, res) => {
  // ...
});

module.exports = router;  // ← Now consistent with other route files
```

